1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,950
Lesson 9: other beams

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:14,093
YA-NEC course, lesson 9: other beams - HB9CV, Quad, Hexbeam and log-periodic. All from the Calculators tab.

3
00:00:14,143 --> 00:00:23,960
HB9CV by Rudolf Baumgartner HB9CV: two driven elements, 103.4 and 95.9 cm at 145 MHz, lambda/8 apart, joined by a crossed phase line.

4
00:00:24,010 --> 00:00:33,760
Real time: 6.32 dBi and F/B 32.5 dB with only two elements. The model has two sources, that is why the SWR card says 'more sources'.

5
00:00:33,810 --> 00:00:38,822
Quad: loops instead of dipoles. Two elements for 14.2 MHz.

6
00:00:38,872 --> 00:00:45,356
Radiator 21.57 m, reflector 22.08 m, 3.17 m apart. SWR 1.17, 7.87 dBi, F/B 10.8 dB.

7
00:00:45,406 --> 00:00:50,429
Three elements: a director is added.

8
00:00:50,479 --> 00:00:55,362
Director 20.93 m: 9.16 dBi and F/B 16.5 dB, SWR still 1.19.

9
00:00:55,412 --> 00:01:01,629
'Multiband': the DK7ZB-style 2-element quad for 20-10 m, all loops on one boom.

10
00:01:01,679 --> 00:01:10,696
On 20 m: SWR 1.08, 6.84 dBi, F/B 15.5 dB. The warning reminds you: one boom means the spacing is ideal for one band only.

11
00:01:10,746 --> 00:01:16,765
Hexbeam 20-10 m with the G3TXQ dimensions and the JN1GLB measurements.

12
00:01:16,815 --> 00:01:26,698
Driven element and reflector bent like a W, bands joined by coax. On 20 m: SWR 1.17, 5.83 dBi, F/B 17.6 dB, in a small turning radius.

13
00:01:26,748 --> 00:01:37,133
Last: the log-periodic dipole array, Carrel method.

14
00:01:37,183 --> 00:01:45,400
Default design 144-432 MHz: tau 0.9, sigma 0.168, 16 elements, 2.78 m boom. Real time: 9.12 dBi, F/B 14.3 dB.

15
00:01:45,450 --> 00:02:27,022
'Calculate with the NEC' sweeps the whole band.

16
00:02:27,072 --> 00:02:36,423
SWR 1.2 at 144 and 1.1 at 432 MHz, gain 7.4 to 10.4 dBi - but a spike to SWR 4.3 near 165 MHz and F/B down to 4 dB at 252 MHz.

17
00:02:36,473 --> 00:02:45,023
The formulas give the start; the NEC sweep shows where to adjust. On HF the same method gives booms of 10 to 27 m.

18
00:02:45,073 --> 00:02:51,023
HB9CV, Quad, Hexbeam, LPDA: four directional families in a few clicks. 73 de IC8TEM
